        "A low-poly 3D office that shows live what Claude Code subagents are doing: who is working, who is waiting for a permission, and which files each one touched.",
      longDescription:
        "Agent Office is a local tool to watch in real time what Claude Code subagents are doing. Each agent has a desk in a 3D office with its status (working, blocked waiting for a permission, finished, errored or no signal). Opening its panel shows the current task, the files it touched, the tool log and its final report. A list view carries the same information as an accessible alternative for keyboard users, screen readers and machines without WebGL.\n\nHow it works: Claude Code runs hooks that forward each event over HTTP to a local server on 127.0.0.1. The server reduces and sanitizes the events and pushes them to the web app over WebSocket. With Docker, the container runs unprivileged with a read-only filesystem and process and memory limits, and publishes its port on 127.0.0.1 only. The access token travels in the URL fragment (the part after #, which the browser never sends to the server) and the web app removes it from the address bar once stored. It also ships a kit of 26 agents and 19 skills, plus an office layout edit mode that is off by default.\n\nActual status: Phase 1 (read-only) is complete. Phase 2, which assigns tasks to agents using your own Anthropic API key, is implemented but has only been tested against a simulated SDK, not the real SDK or a real key. Phase 3 (polish and release) is in progress: it is not yet published to npm and runs from a clone of the repository. The code has Vitest tests and Playwright browser flows, including accessibility tests with axe.\n\n⚡ AI-Assisted — Project co-developed with Claude Code and a team of specialized subagents (orchestrator, pm, architect, ux, backend, frontend, qa, reviewer, security, devops, documenter and others). Every step had human checkpoints.",
      type: "Web App",
      year: "2026",
      tags: agentOfficeTags,
      images: agentOfficeImages,
    },
    {
      title: "Pfinance",
      description:
        "Full-Stack web application and PWA for personal finance management, budgeting, and shared group expenses.",
      longDescription:
        "Pfinance is a comprehensive platform for personal and group financial control. It enables tracking income, expenses, and bank account transfers, categorizing movements, establishing budgets with visual consumption alerts, setting savings goals, and managing group shared debts with automated balance settlement. Built as an installable PWA with JWT authentication, interactive dashboards (Recharts), Excel/PDF data export, and cloud deployment.\n\n⚡ AI-Assisted — Claude Code was a key tool in this project: it accelerated development through responsible vibe coding, suggesting module architecture and global state structure from the earliest stages. It was also actively used for backend security testing (NestJS + Supabase), generating attack scenarios, validating JWT authentication guards, and ensuring critical endpoints were correctly protected against SQL injection and unauthorized access.",
      type: "Web App",
